==In the manga==
[[File:Cabbie Adventures.png|thumb|100px|A Cabbie in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
===Pokémon Adventures===
===={{MangaArc|Sword & Shield}}====
A Cabbie was one of [[Leon]]'s onlookers at [[Hammerlocke]] in ''[[PASS17|Stealth!! Infiltrate the Energy Plant]]''.

In ''[[PASS18|Chomp!! It's Dracovish]]'', a Cabbie who was a {{tc|Macro Cosmos's}} in disguise was sent with his cohorts to [[Route 9 Tunnel]] to dispose of a wild {{p|Dracovish}} that suddenly [[Dynamax]]ed. The Dracovish was saved by [[Marvin]], who used his [[Sniffler]] to stun everyone long enough for him to catch Dracovish and escape. Afterward, they reported their failure to [[Oleana]] and were ordered to stand by in [[Wyndon]].

In ''[[PASS25|Rumble!! The Horrific Darkest Day]]'', two Cabbies were seen informing [[Milo]] that the [[Flying Taxi]] was unavailable due to the mass outbreak of Dynamaxed Pokémon.

===={{MangaArc|Scarlet & Violet}}==== 
[[File:Oscar Adventures.png|140px|thumb|Oscar in [[Pokémon Adventures]]]]
While traversing [[Casseroya Lake]], {{adv|Violet}} and [[Arven]] were nearly eaten by a wild {{p|Dondozo}}. A [[Flying Taxi]] pilot named Oscar (Japanese: '''ヨウヘイ''' ''Youhei''), happened upon the scene and took the two to dry land. Violet thanked Oscar for the assistance, then asked if he knew where the False Dragon {{pkmn2|Titan}} could be found. Oscar directed the two to a nearby island, but warned them to be wary of the many {{p|Tatsugiri}} that lived on it.

